</code></pre> Prefer a DTO as the <code>@RequestBody</code>/<code>@ModelAttribute</code> type.</p> <p><pre><code>const _ = require('underscore');
const SAFE = ['userid', 'password', 'email'];
const user = new User(_.pick(req.body, SAFE));   // isAdmin dropped
</code></pre> With Express, never do <code>new User(req.body)</code> or <code>User.update(id, req.body)</code>.</p> <pre><code>def user_params
  params.require(:user).permit(:userid, :password, :email)  # strong parameters
end
User.create(user_params)
</code></pre> <pre><code>class UserSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
    class Meta:
        model = User
        fields = ["userid", "email"]          # explicit list
        read_only_fields = ["id"]
# Avoid: fields = "__all__"  or  exclude = [...]
</code></pre> <pre><code>protected $fillable = ['userid', 'password', 'email'];   // allow-list
// Avoid: protected $guarded = [];   (everything mass-assignable)
</code></pre> <pre><code>public IActionResult Create([Bind("UserId,Email,Password")] User user) { ... }
// Better: bind to a ViewModel/DTO without IsAdmin.
</code></pre> <pre><code>@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = false)   // fail on extra fields
public class UserDto { String userid; String email; }
// Or mark the sensitive field: @JsonProperty(access = READ_ONLY)
</code></pre> <pre><code>class UserIn(BaseModel):
    model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid")   # reject unknown fields
    userid: str
    email: EmailStr
    password: str
</code></pre>
